    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L03-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "3.3: Thawing Meat",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A piece of meat is taken out of the freezer to thaw. The data points show its temperature \\(M\\), in degrees Fahrenheit, \\(t\\) hours after it was taken out. The graph \\(M=G(t)\\), where \\(G(t) = \\text-62(0.85)^t\\), models the shape of the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l03.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L03-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "3.3: Thawing Meat",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Jada thinks changing the equation to \\(J(t)=\\text-62(0.85)^t + 75.1\\) makes a good model for the data. Noah thinks \\(N(t) = \\text-62(0.85)^{(t+1)}+68\\) is better.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l03.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L03-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "3.3: Thawing Meat",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Without graphing, describe how Jada and Noah each transformed the graph of \\(G\\) to make their new functions to fit the data.",
