      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L03-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "3.3: Thawing Meat",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose there was a third function, \\(j\\), where \\(j(t)=h(t+4)\\). Even without graphing \\(j\\), we know that the graph reaches a maximum height of 66 feet. To evaluate \\(j(t)\\) we evaluate \\(h\\) at the input \\(t+4\\), which is zero when \\(t…",
